--[[
	Server Share - JOINER

	Run this in any game (or the same game) to be dropped into the server that
	whoever is running host.lua is in.

	What it does
	  1. Asks the same public relay (ntfy.sh) that host.lua uses "is anybody
	     hosting?" and only follows a host that answers right now. A leftover
	     announcement from a dead server - or your own earlier session - can
	     never send you anywhere, so with nobody hosting this waits quietly.
	  2. Announces your own username on the "<server topic>_players" topic and
	     then calls TeleportToPlaceInstance, which puts this client into that
	     exact server. That announcement is how the host learns who is coming.
	  3. Queues the session script, which runs in the server you land in and
	     does your half of every trade:
	       - the host's request arrives      -> 2 s later accept the request
	       - the host says its items are in -> 6 s later press accept
	       - both sides press accept        -> press confirm 1 s later
	  4. When the host says it is finished, the session goes back to hunting and
	     follows the next host, arming a fresh session before every teleport.

	Both scripts need the same ROOM, and each side reports what it just did on a
	third topic ("<server topic>_sync") so neither one has to guess.

	The card shows what it found and can be stopped at any time.

	Read the notes next to this file for setup and limits.
]]

